; The Monolith harness. The (select ...) clause picks the real harness when
; monolith is available and a stub otherwise, so plain [dune build] and
; [dune build @runtest] keep working when monolith is not installed. This is
; the mechanism dune provides for depending on optional libraries: neither
; (optional) -- which only affects installation, the executable stays in
; @all/@default and fails the build (this broke CI) -- nor
; (enabled_if %{lib-available:...}) -- not allowed for executables -- works
; here. monolith is therefore NOT a with-test dependency of the package (see
; dune-project / fuzz/README.md).
;
; This executable is intentionally not a test and not attached to @runtest --
; running it means fuzzing (random or afl mode), which is an opt-in activity;
; see fuzz/README.md and fuzz/Makefile.

(executable
 (name main)
 (libraries
  theo
  theo_test_support
  (select
   main.ml
   from
   (monolith pprint -> main.fuzz.ml)
   (-> main.absent.ml))))
